In [[18 BBY]],<ref name="18 BBY">According to ''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]'', the [[invasion of Mon Cala]] took place a year into the [[Darth Sidious|Emperor's]] rule. Since ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates the beginning of Imperial rule to [[19 BBY]], the occupation of Mon Cala, seen in [[Darth Vader (2017) 13|''Darth Vader'' (2017) 13]], took place in [[18 BBY]].</ref> [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]] [[Ferren Barr]] and his [[Ferren Barr's disciples|group of acolytes]] maintained a '''cave refuge''' near [[Bel City]] on the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[planet]] [[Mon Cala]].<ref name="Dark Lord 16" />

{{Loc-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The cave refuge first appeared in [[Darth Vader (2017) 13|''Darth Vader'' (2017) 13]], a [[2017]] comic written by [[Charles Soule]] and illustrated by [[Giuseppe Camuncoli]].<ref name="Dark Lord 16" />

